config DEBUG_CONSOLE_USB
    bool "Debug console over USB CDC-ACM (printf TX mirror + shell RX)"
    depends on COMPONENTS_CHERRYUSB_ENABLE && CHERRYUSB_DEVICE && CHERRYUSB_DEVICE_CDC && FREERTOS
    default n
    help
      Mirror firmware printf/log output to a USB CDC-ACM IN endpoint and source
      FinSH shell input from its OUT endpoint, in addition to the debug UART.
      When disabled, only the UART console is used and behavior is unchanged.
      USB needs the WIFIPLL up (BROM leaves it up at boot) + heap/FreeRTOS, so
      usb_console_init() is called from the app after the scheduler starts.

config DEBUG_CONSOLE_USB_OWN_DISPATCHER
    bool "usb_console provides the usbd_event_handler dispatcher"
    depends on DEBUG_CONSOLE_USB
    default n
    help
      Compile usb_console's own strong usbd_event_handler shim. Leave =n (the
      default) when the app already links a dispatcher (usb_demo's
      usbd_event_common.c or the OTA shim): usb_console registers through it, and
      =y would collide on a duplicate usbd_event_handler /
      usbd_event_register_callback. Set =y ONLY for an app that links no other
      usbd_event_handler.

config DEBUG_CONSOLE_USB_ATTACH
    bool "Attach console into the app's own composite USB device"
    depends on DEBUG_CONSOLE_USB
    default n
    help
      The console does not own the USB device: the app registers a composite
      descriptor carrying a second CDC-ACM (interfaces 2/3, EP 0x84/0x05/0x86),
      calls usb_console_attach() before its own usbd_initialize(), and chains
      events to usb_console_notify_event(). One cable then carries both the
      app's data channel and the shell console.
